  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Cambodia Rural Sanitation Development Impact Bond (DIB)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Cambodia):  .With FY2021 funds, the Cambodia Rural Sanitation DIB activity will leverage the private sector and other stakeholders to support food insecure communities and vulnerable populations to improve access to affordable and sustainable water, sanitation, and hygiene (WASH) products and services. The activity will promote market-sustained and integrated sanitation services, including strengthening the ability of local business owners to provide sanitation products and services, safe fecal sludge management, and better integration of sanitation with handwashing and clean water solutions. This approach has the potential to reach the poorest and most marginalized households in rural Cambodia and close the affordability gap to achieve universal access to improved sanitation. The activity will reach 85 percent rural sanitation coverage by 2023 in 1,600 villages declared Open Defecation Free across six provinces. The activity will work within the integrated Global Food Security Strategy portfolio and integrate WASH activities with agriculture and nutrition activities to increase economic and health outcomes of the targeted communities. Improving access to WASH products and services improves nutrition by reducing the open defecation that contributes to reducing stunting among children and preventing the spread of diseases and contamination of drinking water..The activity falls under the Administration&apos;s priority to grow economic opportunities and prosperity for communities globally and inclusively for all Americans and Cambodians, to end the COVID-19 pandemic, to advance global health security, and to mitigate development and humanitarian impacts. In addition, the activity contributes to Mission Objective 1 (CDCS DO1) &quot;Inclusive and Sustainable Economic Growth Broadened.&quot; . .</narrative>
  </description>
